# (#218) The `at`-qualified interrogatives on the same shape: `what is z
# at L` and `when is z at L` read the name-keyed tape exactly as `prev of`
# does, so a function's call-local writes are visible to a module-level
# query and the module binding is untouched. (The bare `what is z` /
# `when is z` forms are a pre-existing program-wide AOT refusal --
# "temporal interrogative without `at` only supports `prev`" -- not this
# shape's.)
z is 1.0
define u() as:
    z is 0.25
    z is 0.5
    print of (what is z at 11)
    print of (when is z at 11)
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])
print of z
print of (what is z at 11)
print of (what is z at 12)
print of (when is z at 12)
print of (what is z at 8)
